#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:78
msgid "Could not write the uploads .htaccess file — check directory permissions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:103
msgid "Could not update the uploads .htaccess file — check directory permissions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:162
msgid "The built-in theme/plugin file editor is enabled. Any compromised administrator session can use it to inject PHP. Add define( 'DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true ); to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:171
msgid "WP_DEBUG_DISPLAY is on: error output can leak paths, queries, and credentials to visitors. Disable it in production."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: comma-separated list of constant names
#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:188
msgid "Missing or placeholder authentication keys/salts: %s. Weak salts make session cookies forgeable. Regenerate them from the WordPress.org secret-key service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:200
msgid "The database table prefix is the default \"wp_\", which makes blind SQL-injection payloads slightly easier to write. Low priority, but worth changing on a rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:209
msgid "PHP allow_url_include is enabled: include/require can load remote URLs, turning many local-file-inclusion bugs into remote code execution. Disable it."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: PHP version
#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:220
msgid "PHP %s no longer receives security fixes. Upgrade to a supported PHP version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:260
msgid "This path is world-writable: any local process or user on the server can modify it. Tighten its permissions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:286
msgid "A database dump or backup archive is sitting in the webroot, where anyone who guesses its name can download it. Move backups out of the web-accessible tree."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:303
msgid "PHP execution is not blocked inside the uploads directory. Apply the block from the Integrity Sentinel → Hardening screen (Apache), or add the equivalent nginx rule shown there."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:324
msgid "The .git directory is web-accessible: the entire source history (often including credentials in old commits) can be downloaded. Deny access to /.git/ in the server config."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:333
msgid "A .env file is web-accessible — these routinely contain database and API credentials. Deny access to it in the server config or move it out of the webroot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:342
msgid "wp-content/debug.log exists and is web-accessible: it can leak file paths, queries, and plugin internals. Block access to it or disable file logging."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:361
msgid "XML-RPC is enabled. If nothing you use needs it (Jetpack, some mobile apps), disable it — it is a long-standing brute-force and amplification vector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:385
msgid "An administrator account is literally named \"admin\" — the first username every brute-force attempt tries. Create a new administrator and remove this one."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: user login
#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:405
msgid "A new administrator account (\"%s\") was created since the last scan. Verify this was intentional — rogue admin accounts are a standard persistence technique."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:457
msgid "\"%s\" has been closed on WordPress.org — plugins are frequently closed for unpatched security issues and will never receive updates. Find a maintained replacement."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: WordPress version
#: includes/class-is-hardening.php:480
msgid "A WordPress core update (%s) is available. Core updates regularly include security fixes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:35
msgid "eval() of base64-decoded content — one of the most common WordPress backdoor patterns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:41
msgid "eval() of gzinflate/gzuncompress-decoded content — a common obfuscation wrapper for injected code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:47
msgid "eval() combined with str_rot13() — used to obscure injected code from casual inspection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:53
msgid "preg_replace() with the deprecated /e modifier — historically used as a remote-code-execution vector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:59
msgid "create_function() (deprecated) building code from a variable — a classic obfuscated-eval substitute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:65
msgid "Request data (GET/POST/REQUEST/COOKIE) passed directly into a shell-execution function."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:71
msgid "Request data passed through eval(), assert(), or call_user_func() — a common remote-command backdoor shape."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:77
msgid "Error-suppressed include/require of a variable path — sometimes used to quietly load a dropped payload file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:83
msgid "A very long base64-looking string literal assigned in code — often the payload body of an injected backdoor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:89
msgid "Environment/system fingerprinting calls (php_uname, phpversion, disable_functions checks) bundled together — common in webshell \"info\" panels."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:95
msgid "A string strongly associated with a known public webshell family."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-is-heuristics.php:118
msgid "Use of FFI or the dl function to load a native extension at runtime — very rarely legitimate in a WordPress plugin/theme."
msgstr ""

